From 0e48ac8024cf40d9e26d3d4b1e948924c9d5407b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Eden (Doris) build" <doris@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 15:04:17 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] turnip (Doris): keep Eden's 32-bit color images tiled; GPU
 clock/load/temperature report; lock render modes sooner

- tu_image: Eden gives every 32-bit color image a view format list with all 19 formats of its
  size class, BGRA8 among them. On A740 (a7xx gen2, no all-formats-compatible UBWC) a format list
  mixing swapped and unswapped formats forced the image LINEAR, so all of TotK's 32-bit render
  targets and textures (RGBA8, RGB10A2, RG16F, R11G11B10F, R32) were drawn and sampled untiled.
  For Eden ("yuzu Emulator" engine) keep them tiled (still without UBWC). Tiled images ignore the
  swap in CCU and TP alike, so a swapped view reads the image's own channel order; R8G8 vs R16
  reinterpretation still goes linear.
- tu_doris: for Eden, every 10 s the GPU clock and load (sampled every second) and battery, GPU
  and CPU temperatures go to apex_doris.txt with the autotuner's render pass report.
- autotune (profiled): lock a render pass's mode after 10 samples per mode and 10 s (was 15 and
  30 s) and for passes from 0.15 ms (was 1 ms).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
