+             * RGBA8/RGB10A2/RG16F/R11G11B10F/R32 targets were drawn and sampled untiled. Keep them
+             * tiled (still without UBWC). A tiled image ignores the swap in both the CCU and the
+             * TP, so a view with a swapped format reads the same channels as the image's own
+             * format instead of R and B exchanged; Eden only makes such a view when the guest
+             * reinterprets RGBA as BGRA in place. R8G8 vs R16 still needs linear (different tiled
+             * layouts), so that stays.
+             */
